# 1. Ignore everything by default
*

# 2. ...but let git look inside directories, so the rules below can reach files
!*/

# 3. Allow only these files
!.gitignore
!README.md
!LICENSE
!**/README.md
!**/compose.yml
!**/compose.yaml
!**/docker-compose.yml
!**/docker-compose.yaml
!**/Caddyfile
!**/.env.example
!scripts/**
!docs/**
!.github/**

# 4. Never go inside runtime data (the later rules override the allow list)
**/data/
**/config/
**/db/
**/database/
**/repositories/
**/volumes/
**/logs/

# 5. Belt and braces: secrets and databases, even inside allowed folders
.env
**/.env
*.key
*.pem
*.crt
*.p12
id_*
*restic-pass*
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
